From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:25:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/22] Invokers specialized for one vtable slot

Whole-program optimization specializes IL2CPP's VirtualFuncInvoker/
VirtualActionInvoker for a slot that is the same at every call: the copy no
longer reads its slot argument, takes the method from that slot of the object's
class, moves each of its own arguments down one position and writes in as
constants the arguments that were the same at every call. No library can name
such a copy (its arguments are the program's own), so its calls stayed
"call to unidentified native function" with the dead slot register shown as
an argument, the object hidden among them and every argument past the fourth
register dropped.

Such a function is now told by its code (Windows x64): straight-line code,
followed symbolically, that reads the class of its second argument, puts its
own arguments and constants in place and calls or jumps through one entry of
the class's table, the method record from the entry beside it after the last
argument; any instruction whose effect is not known makes it no invoker. The
lifter captures the invoker's arguments by the kinds it reads them as, and the
call becomes the virtual method of that slot on the object, once the method's
signature is checked against where each argument comes from. Where that fails,
the gap names the slot and shows the object only
(__virtual_slotN_arguments_unknown). REWIND_NO_SLOT_INVOKERS turns this off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
